title: The <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**LVP**</span> and the the Banners
subtitle: Due to its militarization, the <span style="color: #FFCC00;">liberals</span> are leaving the the Banners.
view-if: rb_militancy >= 0.04 and not rb_exit and not rb_stay and lvp_formed and lvp_ideology != "Left"
new-page: true
tags: event
on-display: {!  
    var cardEl = document.createElement('div');  
    cardEl.className = "face-figure2";  

    var image = new Image();  
    image.className = "face-img";  
    image.src = "img/reichsbanner_flag.jpg";  

    cardEl.appendChild(image);  
    var contentDiv = document.querySelector("#page #mid_panel #content");
    contentDiv.appendChild(cardEl);
!}
max-visits: 1

= The <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**LVP**</span> and the the Banners

The the Banners has increasingly militarized, acquiring arms, conducting paramilitary training, and attracting a stream of <span style="color: #9B0000;">radicalized</span> <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> members. The <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**LVP**</span> in particular is offended by this, as many of its members originate from the semi-monarchist <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> and even have <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Wardens**</span> memberships. The organization's militarization has provided them with a pretext to sever formal ties with this <span style="color: #000000;">rep</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">ubl</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">ican</span> organization.

- @let_go: Let the <span style="color: #FFCC00;">liberals</span> go.
- @lower_militancy: We must lower the the Banners's militancy.
- @keep_them: Can we convince them that a militant the Banners is necessary for defending the Republic?

@let_go
on-arrival: rb_strength *= 0.95; unionist_relation -= 3; lvp_relation -= 5; lvp_right += 3; pro_republic -= 3; lvp_leave_banner = 1

We have judged that the the Banners's militancy is more important than maintaining a coalition with the <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**LVP**</span>. The the Banners members affiliated with the <span style="color: #FFCC00;">liberals</span> leave, and this may inspire the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] to follow suit.

# TODO: this should make it harder to form Commonwealth coalitions


@lower_militancy
on-arrival: rb_militancy *= 0.5

Bowing to the <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**LVP**</span>'s demands, we reduce the the Banners's military training, thus inducing them to stay.


@keep_them
unavailable-subtitle: They are unable to be convinced at this time.
choose-if: strife >= 3 and lvp_relation >= 55 and lvp_ideology != "Right"
on-arrival: lvp_left += 3; lvp_relation += 3; guild_traditionalist += 3; guild_lvp -= 3; pro_republic += 3

Seeing the strife that has filled the Commonwealth's streets, the <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**LVP**</span> seem to be convinced that it is necessary for the the Banners to be militarized, and will not leave the organization. Unfortunately, many die-hard <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Wardens**</span> members within the party are constantly pressing for a reversal of this policy.